  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"671\" data-end=\"772\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"671\" data-end=\"685\">Method:</strong></span><br data-start=\"685\" data-end=\"688\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">PCR-based VNTR (Variable Number Tandem Repeats) / STR (Short Tandem Repeat) Analysis</span></p>\n<p data-start=\"774\" data-end=\"798\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"774\" data-end=\"796\">&nbsp;Interpretation:</strong></span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"799\" data-end=\"1208\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"799\" data-end=\"935\">\n<p data-start=\"801\" data-end=\"935\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"801\" data-end=\"823\">Chimerism analysis</strong> is used post hematopoietic stem cell transplant (HSCT) to monitor the proportion of donor vs recipient cells.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"936\" data-end=\"980\">\n<p data-start=\"938\" data-end=\"980\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"938\" data-end=\"960\">Complete Chimerism</strong>: 100% donor cells</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"981\" data-end=\"1048\">\n<p data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"1048\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"1002\">Mixed Chimerism</strong>: Presence of both donor and recipient cells</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1049\" data-end=\"1142\">\n<p data-start=\"1051\" data-end=\"1142\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Helps in early detection of <strong data-start=\"1079\" data-end=\"1098\">graft rejection</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1111\">relapse</strong>, or <strong data-start=\"1116\" data-end=\"1139\">engraftment failure</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1143\" data-end=\"1208\">\n<p data-start=\"1145\" data-end=\"1208\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Regular monitoring is essential for post-transplant management.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
